<title>USA: LIN IN DEAL AFTER LONG SEARCH,SHRS SEEN OFF.</title>
<headline>LIN IN DEAL AFTER LONG SEARCH,SHRS SEEN OFF.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>LIN Television Corp, on the auction block for months, drew interest from numerous bidders before taking a $1.7 billion offer from Texas buyout firm Hicks Muse Tate &amp; Furst Inc, arbitragers said.</p>
<p>Hicks said late Tuesday it will pay $47.50 per share in cash plus interest for Lin, owner and operator of eight network-affiliated television stations.</p>
<p>Lin shares finished Nasdaq trade Tuesday at 48-5/8, above the Hicks offer that was likely discounted to reflect takeover speculation that pumped up Lin's share price, the arbs said.</p>
